Description: LuCI app: campus network auto authentication (procd daemon)
 Automatically (re)logs in to the campus captive portal when the WAN
 drops, and exposes a LuCI web UI for status, manual trigger and config.
 .
 Highlights:
  - pure shell + procd, no Python/Lua runtime needed at runtime
  - checks the network every 60 min by default and only then, so a
    short campus outage does not trigger endless login attempts
  - on failure it retries once a minute, at most 5 times, then idles
    until the next scheduled check (no unbounded retry storm)
  - ICMP probes are forced to IPv4 (-4): campus IPv6 often bypasses the
    portal, which would otherwise mask a dead IPv4 session as "online"
  - HTTP probe never follows redirects, so a captive-portal hijack is
    correctly classified as offline
  - self-healing: procd respawns the daemon if it dies, plus an internal
    heartbeat watchdog catches silent hangs
 .
 The web UI is optional: the daemon keeps working even if LuCI breaks.
